[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2977184536","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107586#issuecomment-2977184536","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107586","id":2977184536,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xdDsY","user":{"login":"adamscott","id":270928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3MDkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/270928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott","html_url":"https://github.com/adamscott","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adamscott/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T15:56:22Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T15:56:22Z","body":"> To me personally, it feels like \"not updating the cursor every frame\" should be something that the underlying API does. I also do not believe #103304 is a good way to go about it.\r\n> \r\n> It's inevitable that, for reasons that the developer can't easily handle, the custom mouse cursor changes. Including things such as clickable areas rapidly coming in and out of view, or rapidly moving the mouse cursor.\r\n\r\nThe thing is that I think it's an OK strategy to update the cursor every frame on other platforms. It's just not viable on the Web.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2977184536/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2977197151","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107586#issuecomment-2977197151","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107586","id":2977197151,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xdGxf","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T16:00:29Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T16:00:55Z","body":"> The thing is that I think it's an OK strategy to update the cursor every frame on other platforms. It's just not viable on the Web.\r\n\r\nBy Web being the exception to the _norm_, there _should_ be some underlying mechanism to prevent it. Even if that means not updating the cursor at all or delaying the update, it's much less jarring than the cursor flickering back to its default, unchanged state.\r\n\r\nEither way, the note is a good thing to have.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2977197151/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3743176238","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107586#issuecomment-3743176238","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107586","id":3743176238,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fHFYu","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-13T09:33:12Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T09:33:12Z","body":"It would be good to add a note to https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/inputs/custom_mouse_cursor.html too maybe, to advise that changing the cursor is something best done discretely and not on every frame (it may matter a bit on other platforms too).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3743176238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket"